content:
pgvector adds vector similarity search to PostgreSQL. It supports exact and approximate nearest neighbour search, L2 distance, inner product and cosine distance.

Create a vector column and an index:

    CREATE EXTENSION vector;
    CREATE TABLE items (id bigserial PRIMARY KEY, embedding vector(1536));
    CREATE INDEX ON items USING hnsw (embedding vector_cosine_ops);

HNSW has better query performance than IVFFlat in terms of the speed-recall tradeoff, but it has slower build times and uses more memory. An HNSW index can be created before any data is inserted because there is no training step. Query-time recall is tuned with SET hnsw.ef_search, and a value of 100 is a reasonable starting point.
